codex
I found a concrete remaining fence-parser bypass in both rails: a line such as ` ```not-a-closing-fence` is not a Markdown closing fence, but the shared regex treats its first three backticks as the close. The bytes after it—including a later `verdict: NO-GO`—are ignored, while both readers report canonical input and parse the earlier `GO`. I’m checking whether any existing end-to-end control catches this (the new tests currently cover multiple openers, not a suffixed false closer).
